 and guide the team. Role: Data Analyst-HealthcareLocation: All Persistent LocationExperience: 6 to 10 YearsJob Type: Full-Time Employment What You'll Do: Healthcare Data Analysis \u0026 ReportingAnalyze large?scale US healthcare datasets including claims, eligibility, provider, utilization, and quality dataWrite and optimize complex SQL queries to extract, validate, and analyze healthcare data from relational databasesPerform data validation, reconciliation, and transformation to support accurate reporting for business and regulatory needsHealthcare Data Modeling \u0026 IntegrationWork with Snowflake, MySQL, and related platforms to support healthcare data models, marts, and analytics layersCollaborate with data engineering teams to ensure reliable ingestion and integration of data from source systems (e.g., claims processing, provider systems, eligibility feeds)Support analytics initiatives related to value?based care, population health, quality improvement, and operational efficiencyProcess Mapping \u0026 DocumentationCreate process flows, data lineage diagrams, and system architecture visuals using Microsoft Visio or draw.io for healthcare data workflowsDocument healthcare business rules, data definitions, metrics logic, and reporting methodologiesSupport standardization of metrics aligned with healthcare programs and reporting frameworksStakeholder Collaboration \u0026 CommunicationPartner with business stakeholders including Healthcare Operations, Finance, Clinical, Quality, and Compliance teams to understand reporting needsTranslate complex healthcare data into clear, actionable insights for technical and non?technical audiencesPresent findings, trends, and recommendations to leadership and cross?functional teams Expertise You'll Bring: Bachelor?s degree in computer science, Information Systems, Statistics, Healthcare Analytics, or a related field7+ years Hands?on experience with US Healthcare analytics, including benefits, claims and eligibility dataStrong p